# Private, never commit. See SPEC.md section 5.
#
# The rule these entries enforce: anything shaped by the eligibility profile is
# private, including every artifact produced by acting on it. A leak here is the
# one unrecoverable mistake in this project.

# The real eligibility profile. profile.example.yaml is the committed template.
profile.yaml
profile.yml

# Country-specific sources and the auto-promoted watch list. Both are derived
# from or reveal the profile. Unanchored on purpose: a copy of one of these
# outside config/ leaks exactly as much as the original.
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml

# Runtime state. main is code-only and `data` is an orphan branch written by
# the workflow, so nothing here belongs in a commit on main. The path itself is
# the leak: snapshots/<source_id>/ names a private source, and a directory
# named for the user's embassy names their country. The data branch carries its
# own .gitignore without this line rather than the workflow using `git add -f`.
data/

# Private runtime state. Until P3 builds the encrypted bundle, the snapshots of
# private sources live here in plaintext. From P3 the bundle is decrypted outside
# the working tree, and this line is the second line of defence if that regresses.
.private/
*.decrypted

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.age
*.key
*.age.key
age-key.txt

# Tool scratch
.gstack/
.firecrawl/

# Working plans. A phase plan drives the build and then stops being useful; it
# is a working artifact, not documentation, and a few thousand generated lines
# in the history read as bulk rather than as work. A short summary may be
# committed once a phase lands.
docs/plans/

# Build scratch: task briefs, progress ledgers, review packages. Working
# artifacts of how the code got written, never part of the code.
.superpowers/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# OS
.DS_Store
